    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "SELinux targeted"
          cmd         : "/sbin/sestatus"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*Loaded policy name:[\\s]*targeted[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "Verify /etc/selinux/config is configured with SELINUXTYPE = targeted"
          file        : "/etc/selinux/config"
          regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*SELINUXTYPE[\\s]*=[\\s]*"
          expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*SELINUXTYPE[\\s]*=[\\s]*targeted[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.3.1.11 Ensure SELinux targeted policy is configured"
          info        : "Confiugre SELinux to meet targeted policy, which constrains daemons and system software only.

Without verification of the security functions, security functions may not operate correctly and the failure may go unnoticed. Security function is defined as the hardware, software, and/or firmware of the information system responsible for enforcing the system security policy and supporting the isolation of code and data on which the protection is based. Security functionality includes, but is not limited to, establishing system accounts, configuring access authorizations (i.e., permissions, privileges), setting events to be audited, and setting intrusion detection parameters.

This requirement applies to operating systems performing security function verification/testing and/or systems and environments that require this functionality."
          solution    : "Configure the operating system to verify correct operation of all security functions.

Set the SELinuxtype to the targeted policy by modifying the /etc/selinux/config file to have the following line:

SELINUXTYPE=targeted

A reboot is required for the changes to take effect."
          reference   : "800-53|SI-6a.,800-53r5|SI-6a.,CAT|II,CSCv8|3.3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-6a.,LEVEL|STIGM,Rule-ID|SV-230282r854035_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-08-010450,Vuln-ID|V-230282"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/19886"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
